(5434570, 779769, 79720, '<td valign="top">Thanks, everyone, this feels really good! Love being on the front page of a challenge, and I appreciate you taking the time to leave your comments.<br/> <br/>@ <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=81530" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">jeger</a> <br/>There''s almost never a time when there''s no mist. The less wind the better, of course, but the rush of the water causes an almost constant, impenetrable wall of fog.<br/> <br/>@ <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=23002" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">basssman7</a> <br/>Any time, Ernie. May is beautiful ''round these parts, as you well know. ;-)<br/> <br/>Regarding the location: Yeah, these are the ''Merrican Falls, but as <i>seen</i> from the Canajun side. I had fully intended to get the Horseshoe Falls, but I just never caught a suitable shot, for the reasons I mentioned to Jonathon. See?<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=781857" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/781857.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/781857.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/75000-79999/79720/120/781857.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>@ <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=80104" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">drewhosick</a> <br/> <br/>I tried, my man, I tried. Although they are more impressive, they are a much, much tougher subject to capture.<br/> <br/>for <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=103432" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">hmurmur</a> <br/> <br/>My settings are there in the info, but it was f/9, ISO 100, 16 seconds on the shutter.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-04-13 13:52:40.</i></td>', 'Thanks, everyone, this feels really good! Love being on the front page of a challenge, and I appreciate you taking the time to leave your comments. @  jeger There''s almost never a time when there''s no mist. The less wind the better, of course, but the rush of the water causes an almost constant, impenetrable wall of fog. @  basssman7 Any time, Ernie. May is beautiful ''round these parts, as you well know. ;-) Regarding the location: Yeah, these are the ''Merrican Falls, but as seen from the Canajun side. I had fully intended to get the Horseshoe Falls, but I just never caught a suitable shot, for the reasons I mentioned to Jonathon. See?   @  drewhosick  I tried, my man, I tried. Although they are more impressive, they are a much, much tougher subject to capture. for  hmurmur  My settings are there in the info, but it was f/9, ISO 100, 16 seconds on the shutter.', '2009-04-13 10:05:26.000000', '2009-04-13 14:52:40.000000', 0),
